  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It seems that for remote players, their copy of your avatar's expression parameters are not reset when you switch avatar.\nThis can cause animations to play on the remote end without the avatar user intending to.\nRepo steps;\nHave a 3.0 avatar that sets an expression parameter (say Parameter 5). In my case, it was an int parameter set by a toggle\nHave a second 3.0 avatar that performs an animation based on that same expression parameter (name doesn't need to match, but parameter number does. It may also need to be the same type)\nwhile someone is looking at you;\nIn the first avatar, set the shared parameter\nSwitch to the second avatar\nThe avatar will play the animation triggered by that parameter for the remote user only\nSetting a expression parameter (any of them) seems to clear the stuck parameter (In my case this was done though the expression menu, but a parameter driver component may do the same)",
